-- title:
--   The finite-size brute-force solver has polynomial resource needs
-- statement:
--   For input length $n$ and magnitude bound $U$, the brute-force 3SUM solver uses the resource specification
--
--   $$W(n,U)=n^3+3U+n+20,\qquad C(n,U)=0,\qquad D(n,U)=n^3+3,$$
--
--   where $W$ bounds word magnitudes, $C$ counts additional memory cells, and $D$ bounds call depth. This specification is polynomial: there exist $s,k\in\mathbb N$ such that, for all $n,U\in\mathbb N$,
--
--   $$\max\{W(n,U),C(n,U),D(n,U)\}\le2^s\bigl((n+1)(U+1)\bigr)^k.$$
--
--   This resource property allows the complete brute-force solver to serve as the fallback for sizes below the asymptotic regime.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightBruteThreeSum.lean#L65-L82

